  "term": "congenital rubella syndrome",
  "definition": "Congenital rubella syndrome is a condition in which a fetus is infected with rubella through the placenta, usually during the first trimester of pregnancy after maternal infection. It leads to developmental abnormalities in the newborn, which can include deafness, microcephaly, growth retardation, heart and eye problems, and intellectual impairment.",
